      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Cesare Lombroso (1835\u20131909) was an Italian physician and criminologist
    whose work profoundly influenced the early development of forensic science. A
    pioneering\u2014and controversial\u2014figure, Lombroso attempted to explain
    criminal behavior through biological and anthropological study, proposing theories
    that today are recognized as scientifically flawed and shaped by the cultural
    beliefs of his time.\n"
