  m_text: The museum offers educational activities for students of all ages from
    primary school to college, promoting scientific and cultural learning through
    their unique collections. Exhibits cover topics such as human anatomy, criminology,
    biodiversity, world cultures, and the history of science. All activities use
    a hands-on, investigative approach designed to spark curiosity, support scientific
    thinking, and build key learning skills.
